{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 3 — remediating Gerrit 2336 (LLM-Review -1, Verified -1)\n\n### CI root cause — NOT packaging, and not a flake\n\n`golden-path (clean install)` failed in 52 s on the **end-to-end CLI probe**, one assertion:\n\n    FAIL: show adds exactly comments+description+digest_freshness+inbound_deps+plan_review_health\n      over lean list (got [... 'keyring', ... 'signature'], want [...])\n\n`scripts/probe_rebar.py:552` asserts the EXACT symmetric difference between `rebar show` and\n`rebar list` key sets, in both directions, as a drift detector. Widening `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS`\nchanged the **CLI `rebar list`** shape too — not just MCP — because `list_states(include_body=False)`\nshares `lean_projection`. So the probe was right and the change was under-declared: a **third**\nsurface narrowed. Reproduced locally (141 passed / 1 failed), fixed, now 142 / 0.\n\nThe probe's expectation is now derived rather than hardcoded — the show-only computed fields plus\nthe lean-dropped set INTERSECTED with what `show` actually emits — because\n`authorship_ledger`/`attestations` materialise only once a ticket has signature material, so an\nempty tracker's `show` carries neither. Mutation-checked: shrinking `LEAN_OMITTED_FIELDS` back to\nthe two body fields still fails the probe.\n\n### Findings 1+2 — `ready_tickets` contract: **option (b)**, lean-by-default, documented\n\nChosen over (a) preserve-full-default and (c) bound-only. The deciding fact is that both\nalternatives make the DEFAULT call **fail** on this store: 61 ready tickets weigh 693,556 bytes\nunprojected against a 90,000-byte budget. Turning a working-but-oversized call into a hard refusal\nis a *larger* break than returning less, and (b) keeps the two discovery surfaces agreeing on their\ndefault shape instead of disagreeing. `full=True` returns exactly the previous bytes; `show_ticket`\nis untouched. Recorded as BREAKING (pre-1.0) in `docs/release-notes.md` + `CHANGELOG.md`, with the\nCLI `list` narrowing declared alongside.\n\n### Finding 4 — the budget measured the wrong bytes. Confirmed, and worse than reported.\n\nThe reviewer named one axis (`js_safe_result` quoting 19-digit ints). Measured at this store's\n2,855 rows there are **two**, and the larger was unnamed:\n\n| stage | bytes | delta |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| raw reducer dicts (what the bound measured) | 552,772 | — |\n| after `TicketStateOut.model_validate` | 1,526,327 | **+973,555** |\n| after `js_safe_result` | 1,537,747 | +11,420 |\n\n`TicketStateOut` DECLARES defaults, so `model_validate` **re-adds every field the lean projection\njust dropped** as an explicit `null`/`[]`/`\"\"`. Total under-estimate **178%** — the 90,000-byte\nbudget was in truth passing ~250,000-byte payloads.\n\nFixed by measuring the post-validation, post-`js_safe_result` rows (new `_wire_bytes`); call sites\nnow bound AFTER `model_validate`. Two tests, both killed by a faithful pre-fix revert: an exactness\nassertion (measured == what the client receives) and the regression window — 250 plain rows measure\n49,652 bytes raw (under budget) but reach the client as 135,902 (51% over), so the pre-fix bound\nreturned them.\n\n### Finding 5 — snapshot projection now tested\n\nTwo tests in `tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py` against a REAL pinned view over a real tracker:\nsame query through both backends, identical key sets (kills \"stops projecting\"), and\n`include_body=True` still carries the bodies on both (kills \"projects unconditionally\"). The\n\"cannot drift\" claim is now enforced rather than asserted.\n\n### Finding 3\n\nNo plan-review attestation on this ticket; `review-plan` run to earn one. No `--force`.\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck` (684 files), `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py`,\ncomplexity ratchet `active=39 new=0 increased=0`, and the golden-path probe 142/0.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787951319181371650,"uuid":"431657a3-c2a0-4664-bc30-47c9ad0caf69"}